+# DISPATCH — Trip Slip / Optimize: close the gap to the ratified review experience
+
+**As-of SHA:** `63b86a4` (main, shallow checkout at dispatch time)
+**Live build observed:** `bfa509b6` (production — older than main; several items below are already
+closed on main and the finding is "ship main / verify on live", not "build").
+**Surfaces:** `/itinerary-comparison/:id` (the optimize result page) and the slip it applies to
+(`/plans/:tripId`).
+**Deliverable of the dispatched run:** code changes for the OPEN items only, each landing behind the
+same review-first / §13-honesty / §14–§19 money rules already in force. No schema change without a
+CLAUDE.md ledger row first (Coordination Prevention).
+
+---
+
+## Authority ordering (read before touching anything)
+
+1. **`CLAUDE.md` Locked Decisions** — especially §13 (honest omission, never a guessed figure), §20
+   (publish-time SQL declined; migrations reach prod only via `runMigrations`), §21 ("traveler-facing
+   distance on map surfaces is ALLOWED … users should be able to see the difference"), §22(c)
+   (traveler map = Leaflet/OSM, ODbL attribution, located stops only, no city-center fallback).
+2. **The ratified ledger rows the code cites in-file** — `2026-08-22-slip-optimize-review-first`
+   (the review-first preview strips) and `2026-08-23` (the slip shows baseline + THREE AI variants).
+3. **The mock artifact** Leon flagged (`claude.ai/code/artifact/b39eedaa-…`) — a REFERENCE for intent,
+   **subordinate** to 1 and 2 where they disagree. Where the ratified spec deliberately dropped a mock
+   behavior, that is a *known divergence*, not a build item (see the last section).
+
+If any step surfaces a conflict between these, STOP and escalate — do not fix the doc to match code, or
+code to match the mock, on your own authority.
+
+---
+
+## What is ALREADY built on main (verify on live, do not rebuild)
+
+- **Apply / adopt a proposal is WIRED** — no longer "coming soon / informational only" for the AI
+  variants. `applyVariantMutation` runs `POST /api/itinerary-comparisons/:id/select` then
+  `POST /api/itinerary-comparisons/:id/apply-to-trip`, then navigates to `/plans/:tripId`; nothing is
+  purchased by applying.
+  → `client/src/pages/itinerary-comparison.tsx:955-976` (mutation), `:634` (apply label
+  "Select this plan" / baseline "Keep this plan"), wired through `ProposalColumnContainer`
+  (`:524-641`, rendered at `:1793`) to the apply button in
+  `client/src/components/plancard/ProposalColumn.tsx:183-194`.
+- **Finalize plan + reopen is fully implemented on the slip** (ruling R-F): mutation, owner-gated
+  button, finalized-primary banner, reopen path.
+  → `client/src/components/plancard/SlipView.tsx:462-500` (mutation → `POST /api/trips/:id/finalize`),
+  `:838-845` (the "Finalize plan" button, gated `isOwner && !trip.finalizedAt`), `:517-570` (the
+  finalized-primary banner + "Back to planning"/reopen), and the final-dress flip in
+  `client/src/components/plancard/PlanCard.tsx:903-908`.
+- **Review-first honesty strips** (money-saved / drive-time delta, honestly omitted when the baseline
+  is missing) — `itinerary-comparison.tsx:580-598, 651-736`.
+- **Build-around-a-location anchor modal** — `client/src/components/plancard/BuildAroundDialog.tsx`.
+
+Because production is on the older `bfa509b6`, the first action is a functional check on the live site
+that these four render and behave. If they do not, the fix is **ship current main**, not new code.
+
+---
+
+## OPEN work — lanes
+
+### Lane B — Finalize behavior (Leon's gap #1)
+
+Finalize EXISTS on the slip (above). The gap Leon named ("missing the Finalized Button behavior") is
+almost certainly one of:
+
+1. **Live build predates R-F** — production `bfa509b6` doesn't carry `SlipView.tsx:462-500`. Fix =
+   ship main; then verify: apply a variant → land on `/plans/:tripId` → "Finalize plan" is present for
+   the owner → click → finalized-primary banner takes over, reopen works.
+2. **The optimize→apply hand-off doesn't lead the user to Finalize.** After
+   `applyVariantMutation` navigates to `/plans/:tripId`, nothing signposts Finalize as the next step.
+   If that's the missing "behavior," add the signpost on the slip's post-apply state — do NOT add a
+   second finalize rail on the comparison page (Finalize is owner-gated server-side via
+   `verifyTripOwnership` and belongs to the slip; SlipView comment at `:835-838`).
+
+**Do first:** confirm which of the two it is on the live site before writing code. If (1), this lane is
+a deploy, not a change.
+
+### Lane C1 — proposals must show the ENTIRE plan, not just optimized days (Leon's gap #2)
+
+**Renderer is NOT the problem.** `ProposalColumn.groupRows` already merges purchased anchors +
+variant items and renders **every day present** in day order, marking new/replacement items teal.
+→ `client/src/components/plancard/ProposalColumn.tsx:34-60` (grouping), `:127-170` (per-day render).
+
+The completeness gap is in the **variant payload**: a column shows only what
+`variant.items` contains.
+→ consumed at `client/src/pages/itinerary-comparison.tsx:625-632` (`items: variant.items.map(...)`).
+
+The optimizable set is correctly defined server-side as **all** `in_planning` + `ready_for_checkout`
+items (purchased = constraint-only, emitted as anchors):
+→ `server/services/optimizer-baseline.service.ts:44-55, 171-222` (`loadOptimizerInputs`,
+`baselineItems`).
+
+But variant completeness is **only prompt-requested, not enforced**:
+→ `server/itinerary-optimizer.ts:1288` ("All variants must cover all N days") is a soft instruction to
+the model, whereas protected/purchased items ARE hard-enforced server-side
+(`stripFixedCommitments`, `server/itinerary-optimizer.ts:514-540`). There is **no equivalent
+server-side backfill** that re-adds a baseline optimizable item the model silently dropped. So a
+variant can render a partial plan — exactly Leon's complaint.
+
+**Fix (server, no schema change):** after a variant is generated, reconcile its emitted items against
+the baseline optimizable set; any baseline item the variant neither moved nor replaced is **carried
+through unchanged** (kept, `isReplacement:false`) rather than dropped. This makes "cover all days" an
+invariant instead of a hope, mirroring the protected-items strip that already lives beside it. Add a
+negative test alongside `server/__tests__/` optimizer suites asserting no baseline optimizable item is
+absent from any returned variant.
+
+### Lane C2 — mapped views of the optimized plans (Leon's gap #3)
+
+Today each proposal only gets an **external** "Open in Maps" launcher — no in-app map.
+→ `client/src/pages/itinerary-comparison.tsx:457-514` (`OpenInMapsButton`), used at `:2060` and
+`:2309`. `ProposalColumn.tsx` renders **no** map.
+
+**Fix:** mount an in-app map of each proposal's located stops (§21 permits traveler-facing distance;
+"users should be able to see the difference"). Reuse an existing plan-map rather than authoring a new
+one:
+- **Preferred: `client/src/components/expert/leaflet-plan-map.tsx`** — Leaflet/OSM, **keyless**, which
+  matches the §22(c) traveler-surface convention (located stops only, "X of Y located", **no map when
+  a proposal has no coordinates** — never a city-center fallback) and needs no Google key/referrer
+  dependency. ODbL attribution ("© OpenStreetMap contributors") is REQUIRED wherever it renders.
+- Google-keyed alternatives exist (`components/itinerary/ItineraryMapView.tsx`,
+  `components/plancard/MapControlCenter.tsx`) but tie the map to `VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` + the
+  referrer allowlist; prefer them only if the design calls for Advanced Markers parity.
+
+Placement: a per-column map is dense in a 3-up compare grid — recommend a **toggle** (list ⇄ map) per
+proposal, or one shared map that re-keys to the focused column, over three always-on maps. Confirm the
+layout choice with the mock before building. Honesty rules: connectors are sequence lines, **not**
+routing; no invented distances/durations (§13/§22c).
+
+### Lane D — smaller review-fidelity items (verify, then fix only real gaps)
+
+- **Segmentation recommendation is still "coming soon / informational only"** — this is the multi-city
+  *split* recommendation, a DIFFERENT thing from applying a variant, and is intentionally
+  recommendation-only for now.
+  → `itinerary-comparison.tsx:798-799`. Leave as-is unless Leon rules segmentation-apply in.
+- **Anchor "0 min median" + empty candidate lists** in the Build-around modal read like a **data**
+  gap, not a UI bug — verify with a trip that has geocoded items before touching code.
+- Slip ID / pinned-excluded / trending-popular chips and a name-only custom anchor were mock elements
+  not in the ratified strip set — treat as design questions for Leon, not defects.
+
+### Lane E — checkout payment modal overflow (observed live)
+
+On the paid apply/checkout flow the modal ran taller than the viewport and the Pay button was pushed
+off-screen (Leon's screenshots). Fix = constrain the dialog to viewport height with an internal scroll
+region so the primary action stays visible (`max-h-[90vh]` + `overflow-y-auto` on the content, action
+row pinned). Reproduce on live first; this is styling only, no money-path logic.
+
+### Lane F — Stripe key mode check (observed live)
+
+Production is LIVE mode but the workspace showed `VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY = pk_test_…`. A test
+publishable key on a live deploy (or vice-versa) produces the "request was in live mode, but used a
+known test card" class of failure. **This is a secrets/config check, not a code change**, and touching
+keys is Leon's action, not the dispatched run's: report the mismatch, name the two keys to compare
+(publishable in the client bundle vs the secret key the server charges with), and stop. Do not enter or
+alter any key.
+
+---
+
+## Known divergences from the mock — DO NOT "fix" these
+
+- **No per-stop `[+]/[−]` add-remove ticks in a proposal column.** The mock had them; the ratified Spec
+  C interaction rules **deliberately removed per-item apply** — the column is READ-ONLY, ApplyButton is
+  the ONLY action. Stated in-file: `client/src/components/plancard/ProposalColumn.tsx:12-13`
+  ("NO routing actions, NO per-item apply, NO save-for-later"). Re-adding ticks reopens a closed
+  ruling — escalate, don't build.
+- **`with_expert` items appear in NO column.** Excluded upstream, stated once in the compare header
+  (ruling 8) — not a missing behavior.
+- **Segmentation-apply** (Lane D) is intentionally informational-only for now.
+
+---
+
+## Do-not list (constraints on the dispatched run)
+
+- No schema change without a CLAUDE.md ledger row FIRST (Coordination Prevention); any migration reaches
+  prod only via `runMigrations` on boot (§20).
+- Do not add a second finalize or pin-write rail; reuse the existing owner-gated paths.
+- Do not make the proposal columns writable or add per-item apply (closed ruling).
+- Do not touch Stripe keys, secrets, or any money-derivation path (§14/§18/§19) — Lane F is
+  report-only.
+- Every map renders located stops only, with ODbL attribution, and no city-center fallback (§22c);
+  every figure is server-derived or honestly omitted (§13).
+
+---
+
+## Suggested Replit dispatch line
+
+> Close the OPEN lanes in `docs/dispatches/slip-optimize-punchlist.md` against main (`63b86a4+`), in
+> order B → C1 → C2 → E, obeying the Authority ordering and the Do-not list. Lanes B and the
+> "already built" items are verify-on-live first — ship main before writing code if the live build is
+> behind. Lane F is report-only. Deliverable is a PR per lane with the negative test named in C1; no
+> schema change without a ledger row.
